-- #951 (2026-10-27): the Isle of Thunder (map 1064, 5.2) in the bot travel graph (playerbots DB; beyond AC). Before
-- this file the graph had no node on map 1064, so RoamTransport (#218 / #948) could never route a bot there or back.
--
-- Same generator as #847 lane X phases 2 / 3 (ACs TravelNodeMap model, offline over the 5.4.8 mmaps / DBCs / world DB
-- on a local DB), starting from the test playerbots DB as it stands (every earlier travel-graph file applied):
--  - nodes: the two innkeepers (Horde Uda the Beast 67668, Alliance Isirami Fairwind 70182 - its spawn row has
--    areaId 0, the node takes the area of the nearest spawn, Violet Rise 6583) and the nine spirit healers of map 1064
--    (AC generateNpcNodes flag mask: innkeeper / flight master / spirit healer / spirit guide, AC TravelNode.cpp:1603;
--    map 1064 has no flight master and no TaxiNodes row);
--  - walk links between every two nodes within 2000 yd that the navmesh connects, AC isUselessLink crop;
--  - portal links (type 2, distance 0.1, extra cost 3, path = entrance + exit): the faction camp portals outside the
--    Shado-Pan Garrison in Townlong Steppes (Wowpedia Isle_of_Thunder, API 2026-10-27) - Horde 218462 (spell 138022)
--    -> Dawnseeker Promontory, Alliance 218463 (spell 138024) -> Violet Rise - and the isle return portals 218638
--    (138816, Horde) / 218639 (138819, Alliance) back to the camp portal. No spell has a spell_target_position row,
--    so (as for Tol Barad, #847 phase 3) the exit is the other sides portal. The team of each portal is enforced at
--    route time (TravelNode.cpp TravelNodePath::getCost, #951): a bot never takes the other factions portal.
-- Ids 4200-4399. Every row is linked / calculated = 1 (no regeneration at boot).
